---
// <PipelineFigure> — the two-stage hybrid PSO + DFT workflow, the web version of
// the paper's Figure 2. Plain boxes and SVG arrows drawn from the theme tokens,
// so it follows the notebook/dark toggle and stays sharp at any zoom. No image
// asset, no canvas, no library, and nothing to animate.
//
// Flow: initial swarm → Phase 1 (PSO search, GFN2-xTB) → g_best → Phase 2
// (LBFGS relaxation, PBE+VV10) → refined geometry. The g_best label rides the
// middle arrow, since it is what passes between the two stages.
//
// Layout is a column on narrow screens (arrows rotate) and a row from 900px up.
---

<figure class="pipeline">
  <div class="pipeline-flow">
    <div class="node node--io">
      <span class="node-title">Initial swarm</span>
    </div>

    <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg class="arrow-glyph" viewBox="0 0 40 12"><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="31" y2="6"></line><path d="M31 2 L39 6 L31 10 Z"></path></svg>
    </div>

    <div class="node node--phase">
      <span class="node-tag">Phase 1</span>
      <span class="node-title">PSO search</span>
      <span class="node-meta">GFN2-xTB · tblite</span>
    </div>

    <div class="arrow arrow--labelled" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="arrow-label">g_best</span>
      <svg class="arrow-glyph" viewBox="0 0 40 12"><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="31" y2="6"></line><path d="M31 2 L39 6 L31 10 Z"></path></svg>
    </div>

    <div class="node node--phase">
      <span class="node-tag">Phase 2</span>
      <span class="node-title">LBFGS relaxation</span>
      <span class="node-meta">PBE+VV10 · gpu4pyscf</span>
    </div>

    <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg class="arrow-glyph" viewBox="0 0 40 12"><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="31" y2="6"></line><path d="M31 2 L39 6 L31 10 Z"></path></svg>
    </div>

    <div class="node node--io">
      <span class="node-title">Refined geometry</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="pipeline-caption">
    The two-stage workflow: an initial swarm enters a PSO search scored by
    GFN2-xTB, and its best structure alone is relaxed with PBE+VV10.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .pipeline {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .pipeline-flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  /* ── Nodes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border: var(--hairline) solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    /* Border-only: no fill, so the boxes sit on the island in either theme. */
    background: none;
    text-align: center;
  }
  /* Input and output: the things outside the workflow, held quieter. */
  .node--io { border-style: dashed; }
  .node--io .node-title { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  /* The two computed stages carry the single accent, used as an indicator. */
  .node--phase { border-color: var(--accent-line); }

  .node-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .node-title {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .node-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* ── Arrows ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .arrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 6px;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }
  .arrow-glyph {
    width: 26px;
    height: 10px;
    transform: rotate(90deg);       /* column layout: pointing down */
    overflow: visible;
  }
  .arrow-glyph line {
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.25;
  }
  .arrow-glyph path { fill: currentColor; }
  .arrow-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .pipeline-caption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* ── Wide: lay the stages out left to right ────────────────────────────── */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .pipeline-flow {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: var(--space-1);
      /* Safety net: a narrow island scrolls the diagram rather than crushing it. */
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    .node {
      justify-content: center;
      padding: var(--space-2);
      min-width: 0;
    }
    /* The stages size to their tooling line, which never wraps; the input and
       output boxes take up whatever slack is left. */
    .node-meta { white-space: nowrap; }
    .node--phase { flex: 0 1 auto; }
    .node--io { flex: 1 1 0; }
    .arrow {
      position: relative;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }
    /* The labelled arrow is wider than its glyph, so it buys its own margin. */
    .arrow--labelled { padding-inline: var(--space-2); }
    .arrow-glyph { transform: none; }
    /* Out of flow, so every arrowhead sits on the same centreline. */
    .arrow-label {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: calc(50% + 7px);
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  }
</style>
